# Console configuration.
#
# Anything in a VITE_* variable is compiled into the JavaScript bundle and is public. The WhatsApp
# gateway's URL and API key are server-side infrastructure and must never appear here.
#
# VITE_API_URL is deliberately NOT set for production builds. Left unset, the console calls the API
# on its own origin — which is how it works behind the reverse proxy, on any hostname, with no
# rebuild. Set it only when the API genuinely lives somewhere else.
#
# For local development, put the value in `.env.development` instead of here: Vite loads `.env` in
# every mode, so a value here would be baked into the production bundle too.
#
# VITE_API_URL=https://api.example.com
